{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143/events","html_url":"https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143","id":393718578,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzOTM3MTg1Nzg=","number":1143,"title":"Using new operator on specific class-string doesn't check __construct requirements","user":{"login":"aidantwoods","id":3288888,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg4ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3288888?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods","html_url":"https://github.com/aidantwoods","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aidantwoods/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":486061586,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw0ODYwNjE1ODY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"ee0701","default":true,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2018-12-23T02:56:56Z","updated_at":"2019-01-02T13:18:11Z","closed_at":"2019-01-02T11:58:55Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The following is currently allowed by Psalm, even though it would fail in practice:\r\n\r\nhttps://getpsalm.org/r/ef21737d26\r\n\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n\r\nclass Foo\r\n{\r\n    public function __construct(int $_)\r\n    {\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * @return Foo\r\n */\r\nfunction makeFoo()\r\n{\r\n    $fooClass = Foo::class;\r\n    return new $fooClass;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nPsalm output (using commit d70f853): \r\n```\r\nNo issues!\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nIMO if `$classString` is just known to be a `class-string` then the expression `new $classString` shouldn't be allowed: since the constructor might have requirements (as above), be `private`, or even might be throwing. `class-string` without any more specificity is the `mixed` of metatypes, and you shouldn't really be able to do much with it without running into analysis errors.\r\n\r\nI think a better pattern to enable constructing metatypes might be something like (using the `@template T as ...` notation):\r\n```php\r\n<?php\r\n  \r\ninterface DefaultConstructable\r\n{\r\n    public function __construct();\r\n}\r\n\r\n/**\r\n * @template T as DefaultConstructable\r\n * @template-typeof T $defaultConstructableClass\r\n * @param T::class $defaultConstructableClass\r\n * @return T\r\n */\r\nfunction make($defaultConstructableClass)\r\n{\r\n    return new $defaultConstructableClass;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut this could be generalised to allow other static behaviour too if #1142 is fixed.","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vimeo/psalm/issues/1143/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}